### 画面3: TIER表作成画面

```
Context:
Design the tier list creation/editing screen for "TierHub". This is where users drag and drop items into tier rows to create rankings.

User:
Users who want to rank items (games, anime characters, etc.) by dragging them into S/A/B/C/D/F tiers.

Goal of the screen:
- Allow users to organize items into 6 tier levels via drag and drop
- Provide an item pool at the bottom for unranked items
- Enable saving and publishing the tier list

Screen type:
Editor / Creation screen (iOS-style mobile UI)

Layout & hierarchy:
- Header: Back button, "New Tier List" title, Save button
- Title input field
- Main area: 6 horizontal tier rows (S, A, B, C, D, F)
- Bottom section: Item pool (unranked items)
- Add item button

Components:
- Navigation header with back and save actions
- Text input for tier list title
- 6 tier rows, each containing:
  - Left label with tier letter (S/A/B/C/D/F) with distinct background color
  - Horizontal scrollable area for item thumbnails
- Item pool section at bottom:
  - Label "Items"
  - Grid of draggable item thumbnails
- "Add Item" button (opens item picker)

Visual direction:
- Dark theme (background #121212)
- Tier label colors:
  - S: #FF7F7F (red)
  - A: #FFBF7F (orange)
  - B: #FFDF7F (yellow)
  - C: #FFFF7F (light yellow)
  - D: #BFFF7F (light green)
  - F: #7FBFFF (light blue)
- Item thumbnails are 64x64px squares with rounded corners
- Clean separation between tiers

Constraints:
- Tier rows must be clearly distinguishable
- Items should look draggable
- Sufficient touch targets for mobile interaction

Output expectation:
Generate a tier list editor screen similar to TierMaker.com style, with distinct colored tier rows and a drag-and-drop feel, in dark theme.
```

